  "notes": "{鳴|な}らす means to cause something to produce sound — to ring, sound, or play.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pair: {鳴|な}る (intransitive — the thing itself sounds)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{鳴|な}らしている means 'is ringing/sounding (something)' — an ongoing action.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ベルを{鳴|な}らす: to ring a bell\n- {警報|けいほう}を{鳴|な}らす: to sound an alarm\n- クラクションを{鳴|な}らす: to honk a horn\n- {指|ゆび}を{鳴|な}らす: to snap one's fingers\n- {太鼓|たいこ}を{鳴|な}らす: to beat a drum\n\nIDIOM:\n{名|な}を{鳴|な}らす means to make a name for oneself, to become famous.",
